# Technical stack (enforced)

## Runtime
- **Next.js 15** App Router, **React 19**, **TypeScript**.
- **Server Actions** and **Route Handlers** for data mutations and HTTP — no separate Spring/Express backend.

## Data
- **Prisma** ORM; local **SQLite**, production **PostgreSQL (Supabase)** per SRS C-TEC-003.
- Use **JSON field patterns** compatible with SQLite + Postgres (Prisma extensions / serialization as project already does).

## UI
- **Tailwind CSS** + **shadcn/ui** (Radix) patterns only for new components.

## AI
- **Genkit** + **`@genkit-ai/google-genai`** / Gemini multimodal for STT/Vision/text per SRS.
- Respect **inference logging / model governance** fields in SRS when touching AI paths (`REQ-FUNC-AI-*`, `REQ-NF-031~033`).

## Deploy / limits
- **Vercel** deployment; **60s** serverless ceiling on Hobby — long jobs use **streaming** (`streamText` / UI streaming) and **client-side PDF** for heavy reports per **REQ-NF-001**.
- Large uploads: **direct-to-Supabase Storage** from client when payloads exceed server limits (SRS §3.6.2 pattern).

## Out of scope suggestions
- Do **not** introduce Java/Spring, Kafka workers, or Flutter **unless** SRS changes — this repo is the Next.js app (`pro-ili-smart-app`).
